Each of the above locations will need to be addressed to migrate away from the legacy system. In summary, anywhere the code reads or writes captions.file[...] (currently minimal usage in UI), accesses or mutates the fileLabels array, or uses the paired fileUrls/fileLabels logic, should be refactored to use the new attachment_captions data source. This includes transitioning the UI components (like AttachmentGridViewer and prompts) to fetch and display captions for files from the unified table, and updating the add/delete flows to create or remove entries in attachment_captions rather than in the procedure’s JSON/array fields. By enumerating the above references, we have a roadmap of all the spots in the codebase tied to the old caption/label handling that require changes for the new unified attachment captions implementation.